WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.195
Iapetus is the outermost of Saturn's large moons.

00:03.647 --> 00:16.128
With an estimated diameter of 1,469 km (913 mi), it is the third-largest moon of Saturn and the eleventh-largest in the Solar System.

00:16.808 --> 00:24.974
Named after the Titan Iapetus from Greek mythology, the moon was discovered in 1671 by Giovanni Domenico Cassini.
